data.content:
## .NET 10 OpenAPI Breaking Changes

The root cause is **Microsoft.OpenApi upgraded from v1.x to v2.x**. Here are the breaking changes in your code and the fixes:

### 1. `OpenApiString` / `OpenApiAny` types removed
The `Microsoft.OpenApi.Any` namespace is gone. Examples now use `System.Text.Json.Nodes`:

```csharp
// Old
using Microsoft.OpenApi.Any;
param.Schema.Example = new OpenApiString("1.0");

// New
using System.Text.Json.Nodes;
param.Schema.Example = JsonValue.Create("1.0");
```

### 2. `OpenApiSecurityRequirement` is no longer a dictionary
It no longer inherits from `Dictionary<OpenApiSecurityScheme, IList<string>>`. Use its `Schemes` property:

```csharp
// Old
new OpenApiSecurityRequirement { [oAuthScheme] = scopes }

// New
new OpenApiSecurityRequirement
{
    Schemes = new Dictionary<OpenApiSecurityScheme, IList<string>>
    {
        [oAuthScheme] = scopes
    }
}
```

### 3. `schema.Nullable` removed
Nullability is now a flag on `schema.Type` (which is a `[Flags]` enum `JsonSchemaType`):

```csharp
// Old
property.Value.Nullable = false;

// New — clear the Null flag
property.Value.Type &= ~JsonSchemaType.Null;
```

To *set* nullable you'd use `property.Value.Type |= JsonSchemaType.Null;`.

### Fixed code

```csharp
using System.Text.Json.Nodes;          // replaces Microsoft.OpenApi.Any
using Microsoft.OpenApi.Models;

options.AddOperationTransformer((operation, context, ct) =>
{
    var param = operation.Parameters.FirstOrDefault(p => p.Name == "api-version");
    if (param is not null)
    {
        param.Schema.Example = JsonValue.Create("1.0");           // ← fix 1
    }

    operation.Responses.TryAdd("401", new OpenApiResponse { Description = "Unauthorized" });

    var oAuthScheme = new OpenApiSecurityScheme
    {
        Reference = new OpenApiReference { Type = ReferenceType.SecurityScheme, Id = "oauth2" }
    };
    operation.Security = new List<OpenApiSecurityRequirement>
    {
        new()
        {
            Schemes = new Dictionary<OpenApiSecurityScheme, IList<string>>   // ← fix 2
            {
                [oAuthScheme] = scopes
            }
        }
    };

    return Task.CompletedTask;
});

options.AddSchemaTransformer((schema, context, ct) =>
{
    if (schema.Properties is not null)
    {
        foreach (var property in schema.Properties)
        {
            if (schema.Required?.Contains(property.Key) != true)
                property.Value.Type &= ~JsonSchemaType.Null;     // ← fix 3
        }
    }
    return Task.CompletedTask;
});
```

All three changes stem from the **Microsoft.OpenApi v1 → v2** upgrade that ships with `Microsoft.AspNetCore.OpenApi 10.0`.
